  "details": "Situation: Object with physbone in hierarchy that is attached with parent constraint to the armature (such as hand bone). If there is any physbone in the armature above the bone that the object is constrained to, then the object is world dropped with \"Freeze to World,\" the dropped object still jitters around responding to motion from the avatar.\n\nThis bug does not seem to happen if there is no physbone in the parent armature hierarchy. But it does seem to happen even if the physbone component in the parent armature is disabled. There may be other situations that cause this to happen.\n\nExample of issue: There is a physbone on the avatar's Shoulder.L bone. A separate object with a physbone is using a parent constraint to be attached to the avatar's Hand.L bone. When \"freeze to world\" is activated on that object, the object still moves in response to the avatar moving.",
